  "description": "Subvert i/O Electric equipped bikes partner with your own pedaling efforts in order to amplify the output beyond that of a conventional Subvert courtesy of its battery powered drive unit. Subvert i/O 5 is a Plus specific bike designed to master rocky terrains, offer confidence diving into turns, and be a fully capable off-road adventure companion in all weather conditions. Add to that the power of i/O Electric, and the Subvert i/O HT5 is a force to be reckoned with. Features include a proprietary X6 alloy 27.5\" Plus geometry frame with a tapered head tube. Its ultra cushy ride comes courtesy of its Suntour Raidon Boost Plus fork with 120mm of travel with tapered steerer and a thru-axle, combined with U-40 27.5\" Plus rims, finished with Kenda Havoc Pro 27.5 x 2.8\" 120tpi folding bead tires. Effortless shifting comes courtesy of a Shimano Deore 6000 1X10 Shadow Plus rear derailleur and shifter partnering with its Shimano e8000 38t crankset. Shimano MTB specific e8000 drive unit with 250 watts of power, 70 Nm of torque, and 504 watt battery with a 4 hour recharge from flat form the power plant that allows you glide uphill to do more of what you love, go back down it again.\nSubvert i/O X6 Aluminum frame for Shimano STePS E8000 motor, Tapered head tube\nSuntour Raidon 34mm, Boost LOR-DS 27.5\" Plus fork, 120mm travel, 15mm thru-axle, w/ hydraulic lockout\nShimano STePS E8000 drive unit / 250 Watts / 70Nm Torque, 504 w/h STePS & E8000 battery\nShimano Deore RD-6000, 10-spd, Shadow Plus rear derailleur, Deore 10-spd, 11-42T Cassette\nShimano E8000 crankarms, forged, 38T chainring\nShimano M395 hydraulic disc brakes, 180mm rotors",
